### `@0x8E8` trap (static compare 2026-09-04)

Live Schalke dumps: slots at `club+0x8E8` (Münster / Hannover 96 II) are **16-byte Relationship-like catalogs** — repeating stride, `Permanent` often **79 (0x4F) at +0xD**, `Type` often **5**. That matches AppCake **Relationship** encoding, not FMLE club-affiliation Type (II Club / Feeder Team / …).

II heap candidate (`club@0x160` → uid 3609393) has a **different** layout (near-zero head). **Do not** byte-diff II heap vs `@0x8E8` catalogs for Main/Permanent/PMF — apples/oranges. True FMLE feeders (Kaiser / Legia) also showed empty pointer/UID bridges in archived `affiliates-probe-live` linkAnalysis.

